#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial demonstrates how to build a `Qiskit pattern` for cutting gates"
" in a quantum circuit to reduce circuit depth. For more in-depth discussion "
"on circuit cutting, visit the [circuit cutting Qiskit addon "
"docs](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements {#requirements}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before starting this tutorial, be sure you have the following installed:\n"
"- Qiskit SDK v2.0 or later, with [visualization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) support\n"
"- Qiskit Runtime v0.22 or later (`pip install qiskit-ibm-runtime`)\n"
"- Circuit cutting Qiskit addon v0.9.0 or later (`pip install qiskit-addon-cutting`)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will implement our Qiskit pattern using the four steps outlined in the [docs](/guides/intro-to-patterns). In this case, we will simulate expectation values on a circuit of a certain depth by cutting gates resulting in swap gates and executing subexperiments on shallower circuits. Gate cutting is relevant for Steps 2 (optimize circuit for quantum execution by decomposing distant gates) and 4 (post-processing to reconstruct expectation values on original circuit).\n"
"In the first step, we'll generate a circuit from the Qiskit circuit library and define some observables.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Input: Classical parameters to define a circuit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Output: Abstract circuit and observables\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/depth-reduction-"
"with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/54ed0f13-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Input: Abstract circuit and observables\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Output: Target circuit and observables produced by cutting distant gates to "
"reduce transpiled circuit depth\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We choose an initial layout that requires two swaps to execute the gates "
"between qubits 3 and 0 and another two swaps to return the qubits to their "
"initial positions. We choose `optimization_level=3`, which is the highest "
"level of optimization available with a preset pass manager.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Coupling map showing the qubits that will need to be "
"swapped](/docs/images/tutorials/depth-reduction-with-circuit-"
"cutting/swaps.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/depth-reduction-"
"with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/4fe4af43-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Find and cut the distant gates:* We will replace the distant gates (gates "
"connecting non-local qubits, 0 and 3) with `TwoQubitQPDGate` objects by "
"specifying their indices. `cut_gates` will replace the gates in the "
"specified indices with `TwoQubitQPDGate` objects and also return a list of "
"`QPDBasis` instances -- one for each gate decomposition. The `QPDBasis` "
"object contains information about how to decompose the cut gates into "
"single-qubit operations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/depth-reduction-"
"with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/23e3d25e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Generate the subexperiments to run on the backend*: "
"`generate_cutting_experiments` accepts a circuit containing "
"`TwoQubitQPDGate` instances and observables as a `PauliList`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simulate the expectation value of the full-sized circuit, many "
"subexperiments are generated from the decomposed gates' joint "
"quasiprobability distribution and then executed on one or more backends. The"
" number of samples taken from the distribution is controlled by "
"`num_samples`, and one combined coefficient is given for each unique sample."
" For more information on how the coefficients are calculated, refer to the "
"[explanatory material](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"cutting/explanation/index.html).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*For comparison, we see that the QPD subexperiments will be shallower after "
"cutting distant gates*: Here is an example of an arbitrarily chosen "
"subexperiment generated from the QPD circuit. Its depth has been reduced by "
"more than half. Many of these probabilistic subexperiments must be generated"
" and evaluated in order to reconstruct an expectation value of the deeper "
"circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/depth-reduction-"
"with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/70e2f1b6-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*On the other hand, cutting results in the need of extra sampling*. Here we "
"cut three CNOT gates, resulting in a sampling overhead of $9^3$. For more on"
" the sampling overhead incurred by circuit cutting, refer to the [Circuit "
"Knitting Toolbox documentation](https://qiskit-extensions.github.io/circuit-"
"knitting-toolbox/circuit_cutting/explanation/index.html).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Execute the target circuits (\"subexperiments\") with the Sampler "
"primitive.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Input: Target circuits\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Output: Quasi-probability distributions\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the subexperiment results, subobservables, and sampling coefficients to "
"reconstruct the expectation value of the original circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Input: Quasi-probability distributions\n"
"Output: Reconstructed expectation values\n"
msgstr ""

